
  @expo/agent-cli — get an Expo app running on a device, change it, check it, and ship it

  Usage
    $ npx @expo/agent-cli <command> [options]

  New here? npx @expo/agent-cli help workflow
    what to run in order, the exit codes, and the --json contract

  Commands
    Develop
      dev                     Get this app onto a device: plan it, then run it
      dev:logs                Read what the detached dev server printed
      dev:stop                Stop this project's dev server
      start                   expo start, plus a sync of the agent skills
      stop                    Stop this project's dev server (alias of dev:stop)
      install                 Install packages, and link the skills they ship
      typecheck               Type-check with the project's own compiler
      dev blocks this terminal; dev --detach does not, and dev:logs reads what it printed. dev --plan --ios (or --android, --web) prints a plan without running it; add --json for JSON.
    Understand the project
      status                  Check Expo Go support and whether to rebuild
      doctor                  Run expo-doctor and normalize its report
      inspect:build-log       Say what failed in a build log
      inspect:config-plugins  What the config plugins produced [experimental]
      status compares native changes with the last build: JS-only changes can reload; native changes need a rebuild. Nothing here runs the project.
      experimental commands may change or vanish
    Debug a running app
      smoke                   Prove the app boots, on a device
      navigate                Open a route in the app on a booted device
      runtime:eval            Evaluate JavaScript in the running app
      runtime:errors          Collect runtime errors over a time window
      runtime:tree            What is on screen, ready for a tap
      runtime:tap             Tap the element carrying a testID
      runtime:type            Type into the input with a testID
      runtime:reload          Reload the app onto the code on disk now
      runtime:stop            Stop the app on the device it runs on
    Create a project
      new                     Create a new Expo project without a terminal
    Deployment
      deploy                  Ship the web app, or launch the native one
    Agent setup
      agents:setup            Set up Expo agents in a project or user home
      skills:sync             Link the installed packages' skills
      skills:list             List the skills the installed packages ship
      skills:show             Print the SKILL.md of a package
      skills:clean            Remove the managed skill links
      agents:setup --yes --agent <agent> --json runs without prompting; --no-plugins skips plugin installation.
    Learn
      help                    Learn the workflow, or one command's help
      docs:sync               Download the Expo docs as .md files to grep
      docs:search             Search the local Expo docs, with file and line
    Feedback
      feedback                Send feedback to the Expo team
    Account
      login, logout, register, whoami
      No project needed: they act on the ~/.expo session the expo and eas CLIs share.
    Expo CLI (fallback to npx expo <command>)
      run, run:ios, run:android, prebuild, config, export, export:web,
      export:embed, serve, customize, lint

  Options
    --version, -v   Version number
    --help, -h      Usage info

  The options, examples and JSON keys of one command
    $ npx @expo/agent-cli status --help

